Tough, but slow.

I haven't been killed by a mimic in many dozen games.  I find them
quite easy, actually, if
one takes the following precautions:

1)  Enter a shop with telepathy and wearing a blindfold. This allows
you to identify them. They are not aware of me, but I am aware of them.


2) Kill them with a polearm.  A polearm allows me to keep them at a
distance. If they close the gap, I simply step away, for even at normal
speed I am faster than they.  It also means that I don't throw away
missile weapons which I will have to buy back.

3) If I don't have telepathy, I use "s" to search the shop thoroughly
before I do anything else. If I find a mimic, use polearm and greater
speed as above.

4) If by mischance I *DO* get stuck to a mimic, simply engrave
"Elbereth" or drop a scroll of scare monster. The creature will
immediately release me. Then run away and use polearm as above.

